<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Franconia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> is an administrative region in the north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> as its seat. It covers the lands of the former prince-bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> and the principality of Bayreuth, which passed to Bavaria between 1802 and 1810. Its towns include Bamberg, Bayreuth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and Hof.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-franconia.jpg" alt="Upper Franconia" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Oberfranken.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
